course: dictionary
lesson: 3947
title: Fund: money and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fund is money saved or collected for a special purpose. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits. «Many zoos fund rangers and scientists in places like Kenya» means the zoos give the money that pays for them.
explain: Funds, with an s, usually means money that is ready to spend. Short of funds means you do not have enough money. Schools often raise funds, which means collecting money, for things like a new roof.
explain: Fund can also mean a large supply of something. «A fund of stories» is a great many stories ready to tell. It is the same idea as a store you can keep taking from.
explain: A check helps you. Swap your meaning into the sentence. If «a fund of stories» becomes «a large supply of stories» and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A fund is money saved or collected for a special purpose.
fact: «An emergency fund» is money kept for unexpected costs, such as a £250 repair.
fact: «A rainy day fund» is money saved for bad surprises, because a rainy day means a time of trouble.
fact: To fund something means to give the money that pays for it.
fact: «A fund of jokes» means a large supply of jokes.
exercise: «Many zoos fund rangers and scientists in places like Kenya.» What does fund mean here? | Forget about them | Hide them from visitors | *Give the money that pays for them | Count how many there are
exercise: «An emergency fund is money kept for unexpected costs.» Which of these is an unexpected cost? | Your weekly bus fare | *A boiler that breaks suddenly in winter | A birthday party you planned for months
exercise: Ruth says, «Grandad has a fund of stories.» What does this mean? | *He knows a large supply of stories | He reads very slowly | He is short of money | He has lost all his books
test: «The school fund paid for the new playground.» What is the school fund? | A map of the school grounds | A list of the teachers' names | *Money saved or collected for a special purpose | A cupboard full of pencils
test: Ahmed says, «We are short of funds for the trip.» What does short of funds mean? | We have plenty of spare money | We have lost the trip | We have too many buses | *We do not have enough money to pay
exam: «An index fund spread £100 over 100 companies.» How much money went into each company? | £10 | £0.10 | £100 | *£1
